<EzizeLegalLayout title="Terms of use" description="The rules for accounts, EZ coins, generations, membership, and use of the EZIZE service." active="terms">
  <p class="plain-summary"><strong>Plain-English summary:</strong> EZIZE sells prepaid pulls from an authored image probability machine. One EZ coin pays for one completed generation. Use the service lawfully, keep your account secure, and read the output license before using an EZ commercially. The sections below are the full EZIZE terms.</p>

  <h2>1. Operator and agreement</h2>
  <p>EZIZE is a HobFarm service operated by Kris Reynolds in Las Vegas, Nevada. “HobFarm,” “EZIZE,” “we,” and “us” refer to that operator and service. By creating an account, buying EZ coins, starting a membership, or generating an EZ, you agree to these terms, the <a href="/ezize/privacy/">EZIZE Privacy Notice</a>, the <a href="/ezize/refunds/">EZIZE Refund Policy</a>, and the <a href="/ezize/license/">EZIZE Output License</a>.</p>
  <p>You must be legally able to enter this agreement. If you use EZIZE for a business or another organization, you confirm that you have authority to bind it.</p>

  <h2>2. What EZIZE does</h2>
  <p>EZIZE is a probability machine for collectible Cake, Critter, and Character images. The machine makes authored, weighted selections under a versioned rule set and sends the resolved instruction to an AI image renderer. A successful pull produces a high-resolution PNG, unique EZ ID, filename, timestamp, form, persona, Generation Path Odds, and account receipt.</p>
  <p>Generation Path Odds are the theoretical chance that the same version of EZIZE would make the same sequence of weighted selections again. They do not mean an identical pixel-for-pixel image would render again, measure copyright uniqueness, or describe how many images were generated, sold, or made available.</p>

  <h2>3. Accounts and access</h2>
  <p>An account is free and uses passwordless access through a verified email address. You are responsible for access to that email account, the accuracy of the information you provide, and activity under your EZIZE account. Tell HobFarm promptly through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> if you believe the account has been compromised.</p>
  <p>Logging out does not remove an unused coin balance. Completed paid EZs are made recoverable through the account, subject to the retention and availability terms below.</p>

  <h2>4. EZ coins</h2>
  <p>One EZ coin pays for one complete EZ generation. Coins are internal prepaid service credit. They are not cryptocurrency, blockchain tokens, securities, an investment, legal tender, or a stored-value account. They cannot be withdrawn as cash. Current packs are 5 coins for $5, 10 for $9, 20 for $17, 50 for $42, and 100 for $80, in U.S. dollars.</p>
  <p>A coin is consumed when a generation completes successfully. If a qualifying technical failure prevents the service from delivering a completed EZ, the coin should be restored or replaced under the <a href="/ezize/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>. Starting another pull or changing your mind after a successful result does not undo the completed service.</p>

  <h2>5. HobFarm Club grants</h2>
  <p>HobFarm Club costs $5 per month. Each successfully paid month adds five EZ coins to the member's account. Coins stack with prior balances and with separately purchased packs. Canceling stops future billing and future monthly grants; it does not erase unused coins or completed EZs already associated with the account. If membership restarts, monthly grants resume after successful payments.</p>
  <p>Failed, reversed, refunded, or disputed membership payments do not earn a monthly coin grant. HobFarm may correct duplicate or mistaken grants that are not supported by a successful payment.</p>

  <h2>6. Payments</h2>
  <p>Stripe processes payments and may store payment methods, billing details, and subscription records under its own terms and privacy notice. HobFarm does not store full card numbers or card security codes. Prices, taxes, and the amount charged are shown before checkout. You authorize the displayed charge when you confirm a purchase or recurring membership.</p>

  <h2>7. Outputs and license</h2>
  <p>A successful paid pull grants the rights described in the <a href="/ezize/license/">EZIZE Output License</a> for that specific output. The license does not transfer the EZIZE system, HobFarm brands, private generation data, or another person's EZ. AI-assisted output may not qualify for copyright protection in every jurisdiction, and HobFarm does not promise copyrightability, exclusivity, or pixel-level uniqueness.</p>
  <p>HobFarm may display or curate selected EZs to explain or promote the machine, identify an output by its EZ ID, and demonstrate possible derivatives. The license page explains that limited retained permission and how to request reasonable attribution or privacy adjustments.</p>

  <h2>8. Prohibited use</h2>
  <p>You may not use EZIZE to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break the law, infringe another person's rights, or facilitate fraud, threats, harassment, exploitation, or abuse;</li>
    <li>attempt to extract private prompts, seeds, genomes, traces, schemas, weights, pack data, source code, credentials, or security controls;</li>
    <li>scrape, automate, overload, probe, reverse engineer, or interfere with the service except where applicable law gives a right that cannot be waived;</li>
    <li>resell account access, manipulate balances, evade payment, or misrepresent EZ coins as cryptocurrency, investments, or financial assets;</li>
    <li>claim that an EZ ID proves copyright, exclusive uniqueness, human authorship, endorsement, or ownership of the EZIZE system.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Availability, changes, and account action</h2>
  <p>EZIZE depends on hosting, payment, email, storage, and AI rendering services. HobFarm may maintain, change, pause, replace, or discontinue parts of the service. Changes to renderers or rule-set versions may change future results without changing the record attached to an earlier pull.</p>
  <p>HobFarm may restrict or close an account when reasonably necessary for security, fraud prevention, legal compliance, payment disputes, or serious or repeated violations of these terms. When practical, HobFarm will provide notice and a way to recover eligible paid outputs. Coin balances and refunds remain subject to payment status, fraud review, the Refund Policy, and applicable law.</p>

  <h2>10. Disclaimers and limits</h2>
  <p>EZIZE is provided on an “as available” basis. To the extent permitted by law, HobFarm does not promise uninterrupted operation, a particular aesthetic result, resale value, market demand, copyright protection, or compatibility with a particular downstream product or platform. Nothing in these terms excludes a warranty or consumer right that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
  <p>To the extent permitted by law, HobFarm is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from EZIZE. HobFarm's aggregate liability for a claim related to a paid purchase will not exceed the amount you paid to HobFarm for the purchase giving rise to that claim. This limit does not apply where the law forbids it.</p>

  <h2>11. Governing law and changes</h2>
  <p>Nevada law governs these terms, without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except where mandatory consumer law in your location applies. Disputes may be brought in courts with jurisdiction in Clark County, Nevada, unless applicable law gives you another required forum.</p>
  <p>HobFarm may update these terms as EZIZE changes. Material changes will be announced through an appropriate service message or account notice and will apply prospectively from the stated effective date. Continued use after that date means you accept the revised terms.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>Use the <a href="/contact/">HobFarm contact page</a> for questions about these terms, account access, a purchase, or a legal request. Include the account email and relevant EZ ID or receipt reference, but never send a passwordless sign-in link or complete card details.</p>
